# Q3. Memory Bottleneck Debugging

## Given

Code = 5 MB

Heap = 150 MB

Stack = 1 MB/thread

Threads = 25

RAM = 2 GB

---

## Memory Usage

Code

5 MB

Heap

150 MB

Stacks

25 × 1 MB = 25 MB

Total

180 MB

---

## Root Cause

Although total memory usage is only 180 MB, the application experiences frequent page faults because:

- Large heap causes poor locality.
- Threads access different memory pages.
- Working set exceeds cache efficiency.
- Memory fragmentation increases page faults.

---

## Optimization 1

Reduce heap usage.

- Free unused memory.
- Use memory pooling.

---

## Optimization 2

Reduce thread count.

Use a thread pool instead of creating many threads.

---

## Conclusion

Performance degradation is caused by excessive page faults and inefficient memory access patterns.
